    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1950-p26.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Rearranging and using the product rule for logarithms gives \\[ \\begin{aligned} &\\log_{10}m+\\log_{10}n\\\\ &=\\log_{10}(mn)=b. \\end{aligned} \\] Therefore \\(mn=10^b,\\) so \\(m=\\dfrac{10^b}{n}.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Move \\(\\log_{10}n\\) to the left side",
        "Combine the two logarithms and then exponentiate with base \\(10\\)"
      ],
